  /**
   * Add a product to the customer's wishlist for future purchase consideration.
   *
   * This operation allows authenticated customers to save products they are interested in for potential future purchase. The product is added to their personal wishlist, which is automatically created upon account registration.
   *
   * **Business Rules**
   *
   * - Each customer has exactly one personal wishlist (section 433)
   * - A product can only appear once in a wishlist; duplicate additions return a conflict error
   * - Only the wishlist owner can add items to their wishlist (section 312)
   * - The referenced product must exist and be available on the platform
   * - Products are automatically removed from all wishlists when deleted by the seller (sections 179, 442, 539)
   *
   * **Access Control**
   *
   * - The authenticated customer must own the specified wishlist
   * - Administrators cannot access individual customer wishlists (section 312)
   *
   * **Response**
   *
   * Returns the created wishlist item record with timestamps and references to the wishlist and product.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param wishlistId UUID identifier of the customer's wishlist (global scope)
   * @param body Product identifier to add to the wishlist. The product must exist and be available on the platform.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor customer
   * @x-autobe-specification 1. Validate the authenticated customer owns the wishlist referenced by {wishlistId}. Return 403 if access denied (section 312).
   * 2. Verify the wishlist exists and is not soft-deleted (deleted_at IS NULL).
   * 3. Verify the referenced product exists and is not soft-deleted.
   * 4. Check for duplicate: query ecommerce_wishlist_items where ecommerce_wishlist_id = {wishlistId} AND ecommerce_product_id = {productId} AND deleted_at IS NULL. If exists, return 409 Conflict.
   * 5. Generate UUID for new wishlist item id.
   * 6. Insert into ecommerce_wishlist_items with ecommerce_wishlist_id, ecommerce_product_id, created_at = now(), updated_at = now(), deleted_at = NULL.
   * 7. Return the created wishlist item with all fields.
   *
   * Edge cases:
   * - Invalid wishlistId format: 400 Bad Request
   * - Wishlist not found: 404 Not Found
   * - Product not found: 404 Not Found
   * - Product already in wishlist: 409 Conflict
   * - Unauthorized access (wishlist belongs to different customer): 403 Forbidden
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post()
  public async create(
    @CustomerAuth()
    customer: CustomerPayload,
    @TypedParam("wishlistId")
    wishlistId: string & tags.Format<"uuid">,
    @TypedBody()
    body: IEcommerceWishlistItem.ICreate,
  ): Promise<IEcommerceWishlistItem> {
    try {
      return await postEcommerceCustomerWishlistsWishlistIdItems({
        customer,
        wishlistId,
        body,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Retrieve a paginated list of products saved in a customer's wishlist.
   *
   * This operation returns wishlist items belonging to the specified wishlist, including product details such as name, images, and current pricing. The endpoint supports filtering, sorting, and cursor-based pagination for efficient browsing of large wishlists.
   *
   * **Access Control**
   *
   * Only the authenticated customer who owns the wishlist can access this endpoint. The system validates that the current customer ID matches the wishlist owner before returning any data. Administrators cannot view individual customer wishlists as this data is private.
   *
   * **Automatic Cleanup**
   *
   * Wishlist items referencing deleted products are automatically removed by the system and will not appear in results. If a seller deletes a product, all wishlist items referencing that product are immediately purged across all customers.
   *
   * **Pagination**
   *
   * The response uses cursor-based pagination. Include cursor and limit parameters in the request body to navigate through pages. Maximum items per page is enforced by business rules to prevent excessive data retrieval.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param wishlistId Unique identifier of the wishlist to retrieve items from (UUID format).
   * @param body Search criteria including pagination parameters (cursor, limit), sorting options, and optional filters for product name or status.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor customer
   * @x-autobe-specification Query ecommerce_wishlist_items table with pagination and filtering. First validate that the authenticated customer owns the wishlist by checking ecommerce_wishlists.ecommerce_customer_id matches the current customer. Apply soft-delete filter to exclude items where deleted_at is not null. Join with ecommerce_products to fetch product details (name, images, current price). Filter by product name or status if provided in request. Implement cursor-based pagination using created_at as the cursor field. Return summary projection excluding full product details to optimize list performance. Enforce pagination limits from business rules (maximum items per page).
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Patch()
  public async index(
    @CustomerAuth()
    customer: CustomerPayload,
    @TypedParam("wishlistId")
    wishlistId: string & tags.Format<"uuid">,
    @TypedBody()
    body: IEcommerceWishlistItem.IRequest,
  ): Promise<IPageIEcommerceWishlistItem.ISummary> {
    try {
      return await patchEcommerceCustomerWishlistsWishlistIdItems({
        customer,
        wishlistId,
        body,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Retrieve a single wishlist item with its associated product details.
   *
   * This operation fetches a specific product saved in a customer's wishlist by the wishlist item identifier. The response includes the complete wishlist item record along with the current product information, allowing customers to review saved products before purchase.
   *
   * **Access Control**
   *
   * Only the authenticated customer who owns the wishlist can access this endpoint. The system validates that the requesting customer matches the wishlist owner before returning the item. Unauthorized access attempts are rejected with an access denied error.
   *
   * **Product Availability**
   *
   * If the referenced product has been deleted by the seller, the wishlist item will not be found since deleted products are automatically removed from all wishlists. This ensures customers only see currently available products.
   *
   * **Relationships**
   *
   * The response includes the complete product entity with current pricing, availability status, and product details. Product snapshots are not included in this operation.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param wishlistId Unique identifier of the customer's wishlist (global scope).
   * @param itemId Unique identifier of the wishlist item to retrieve (global scope).
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor customer
   * @x-autobe-specification 1. Authenticate the requesting customer from session token.
   * 2. Validate the wishlist exists and belongs to the authenticated customer (ecommerce_wishlists.ecommerce_customer_id = customer.id).
   * 3. Query ecommerce_wishlist_items table for the item with matching id and ecommerce_wishlist_id.
   * 4. Verify the item's deleted_at is NULL (not soft-deleted).
   * 5. Join with ecommerce_products to retrieve current product details.
   * 6. Validate the product's deleted_at is NULL (product not deleted by seller).
   * 7. Return the wishlist item with embedded product information.
   * 8. If wishlist not found or doesn't belong to customer, return 404 Not Found.
   * 9. If item not found in wishlist, return 404 Not Found.
   * 10. If product was deleted, the item won't exist (automatic cleanup), return 404 Not Found.
   * 11. Use UUID validation for both path parameters.
   * 12. Apply customer data isolation - never expose other customers' wishlist items.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
